# ep9 code owners (docs/plan/12-governance.md section 4; docs/adr/README.md section 4, P-4).
#
# The owner is the GitHub account that owns this repository. It is the only human on the team;
# AI agents do the work and open their PRs from the same account. GitHub does not let a PR author
# approve their own PR, so branch protection must NOT require code-owner review: it would block
# every PR. This file:
#   1. names the paths whose PRs need more than the default review (docs/plan/12-governance.md 4.2),
#   2. is read by the review checklist and, later, by the ADR lint (cargo xtask),
#   3. makes GitHub show the owner on these paths.
# Syntax: paths start at the repo root; the last matching line wins; no "!" negation.

# Contract crates (docs/plan/10-quality.md section 6) and ep9_platform (H28, unsafe OS code).
# Crates that do not exist yet are listed so that they are owned from their first commit.
/crates/ep9_value/        @Brooooooklyn
/crates/ep9_heap/         @Brooooooklyn
/crates/ep9_platform/     @Brooooooklyn
/crates/ep9_bytecode/     @Brooooooklyn
/crates/ep9_vm/           @Brooooooklyn
/crates/ep9_frontend/     @Brooooooklyn
/crates/ep9_masm/         @Brooooooklyn
/crates/ep9_baseline/     @Brooooooklyn
/crates/ep9_opt/          @Brooooooklyn
/crates/ep9_unit/         @Brooooooklyn
/crates/ep9_aot/          @Brooooooklyn
/crates/ep9_facts/        @Brooooooklyn

# Engine crates with their own ADR rule: ep9_math is the one Rust Math (H36: the same float bits
# on every target); ep9_builtins uses only the builtin ABI (H20) and has no unsafe code.
/crates/ep9_math/         @Brooooooklyn
/crates/ep9_builtins/     @Brooooooklyn

